Experiment I-B: VG-150 PredCls relation-depth component study. This replaces
the former relation-token classifier. Every graph node is one ground-truth
object and every supervised example is an ordered object pair. The experiment
is intentionally PredCls-only and does not test object recognition. Experiment
I-A is the paper's object-grounding study; complete PredCls/SGCls/SGDet
evaluation belongs to Experiment IV.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --vg_root VG_ROOT
  --output_dir OUTPUT_DIR
  --feature_mode {raw_backbone,official_features,proxy_smoke}
  --backbone BACKBONE
  --reasoning {gcn,gat,transformer}
  --depths DEPTHS [DEPTHS ...]
  --seeds SEEDS [SEEDS ...]
  --train_samples TRAIN_SAMPLES
  --test_samples TEST_SAMPLES
  --epochs EPOCHS
  --hidden_dim HIDDEN_DIM
  --negative_ratio NEGATIVE_RATIO
  --gradient_accumulation_steps GRADIENT_ACCUMULATION_STEPS
  --roi_chunk_size ROI_CHUNK_SIZE
  --eval_pair_chunk_size EVAL_PAIR_CHUNK_SIZE
  --amp, --no-amp       Use CUDA mixed precision; ignored on CPU.
  --minimum_pvr_checked MINIMUM_PVR_CHECKED
  --learning_rate LEARNING_RATE
  --weight_decay WEIGHT_DECAY
  --cache_dir CACHE_DIR
  --device DEVICE
